# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto

# A .kbar is a zip. text=auto guesses by content and would almost certainly
# guess right, but "almost certainly" is not what you want protecting an
# archive: one normalised byte and the import fails with nothing to point at.
*.kbar binary

# The compiled effect plug-in. Same reasoning as the .kbar: a DLL must not be
# line-ending normalised, and text=auto should not be left to guess at it.
*.aex binary

# Shell scripts must keep LF even when checked out on Windows, or bash
# rejects them with a \r it cannot see.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The macOS plug-in bundle - every file in it, not just the Mach-O. The
# ad-hoc signature hashes file contents, and _CodeSignature/CodeResources and
# Info.plist are text: let text=auto give either of them CRLF on a Windows
# checkout and the signature no longer matches, so the effect is refused on
# Apple Silicon without ever saying why.
plugins/vr_color_gradients_3d/ChromaVRGradient3D.plugin/** binary
*.rsrc binary
